ef 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aa193fd-3e1c-5c64-a1e5-49de27dc86d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315800} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba23914-953a-5985-91e2-6cfb73dc742e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25ecade8-fcdb-5fbb-91a9-b63ee8dd4d3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{48(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315331} {:answer/id #uuid "76dc7d98-a1d1-5857-bd88-226267ef6d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315789} {:answer/id #uuid "9e38dfcb-edf6-509c-b949-c49211760623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{48(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316006} {:answer/id #uuid "d749d0ae-a22d-5ed1-be30-0b1f60b7b732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e38dfcb-edf6-509c-b949-c49211760623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{48(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316006} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2d45990-077c-5ce4-90c0-dbfc23fdd7cd" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317088} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ad2f00c-b8bd-52f8-8259-63fb31e76519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315457} {:answer/id #uuid "4a00f21f-5599-5f72-8b88-407db5f68046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315542} {:answer/id #uuid "54a4284d-878d-5837-bf31-4feba40875d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "periodic" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315604} {:answer/id #uuid "d22fec79-5cae-53ba-a6d9-86446d3ff8fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d22fec79-5cae-53ba-a6d9-86446d3ff8fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316295} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa42d7e4-a254-55bd-8ac0-ef1e79e9d268" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7403504-1eb6-58c7-80a7-8e8d0a72b009" :question/math-academy-id "q-343380" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}$ defined on $[-2,2).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $4$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}∼-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{24(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}∼-2x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and we are already given the coefficients for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{24(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-2,2).$ \nTherefore, the $4$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{24(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2}))\\text{d}t \\\\ {[-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}]}_{0}^{x} & ∼[-2t]_{0}^{x}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{24(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot [\\frac{2}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2})]_{0}^{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3} & ∼-2x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{48(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
